// COVERS BigQueryLexerGrammar: BigQuery, projectId, defaultDataset, proxyHost, proxyPort
// COVERS BigQueryFunctionLexerGrammar: BigQueryFunction, functionName, function, ownership, Deployment, identifier, description, activationConfiguration, BigQueryFunctionDeploymentConfiguration, activationConnection, stage
//
// Two unrelated grammars that happen to share a vendor, in the two sections that route to
// them: BigQueryLexerGrammar is the relational datasource spec (###Connection), and
// BigQueryFunctionLexerGrammar is the function activator, whose section is `###BigQuery`
// (BigQueryFunctionGrammarParserExtension.java:38, `NAME = "BigQuery"` -- NOT
// `###BigQueryFunction`, which is the trap).
//
// Connection syntax from TestBigQueryConnectionGrammarRoundtrip; activator syntax from
// TestBigQueryFunctionRoundtrip.
//
// `stage` is reachable only as an identifier. BigQueryFunctionParserGrammar.g4:67 defines a
// `stage` rule, but `definition` (line 29) admits only bigQueryFunction and deploymentConfig,
// and `deploymentConfig` (line 58) contains just activationConnection -- nothing references
// the rule, so `stage : '...';` cannot be written inside any element. The token survives
// only through the `identifier` alternation (line 19), so the fixture names an element with
// it. That is also why `BigQueryFunctionDeploymentConfiguration` needs its own top-level
// element: it is an element keyword, not a field.
//
// Note ownership is OPTIONAL for BigQueryFunction (validateAndExtractOptionalField,
// BigQueryFunctionTreeWalker.java) whereas MemSqlFunction requires it -- the two grammars
// look identical and are not.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::bq::Conn
{
   store: fixture::bq::Db;
   type: BigQuery;
   specification: BigQuery
   {
      projectId: 'proj1';
      defaultDataset: 'dataset1';
      proxyHost: 'proxyHost1';
      proxyPort: 'proxyPort1';
   };
   auth: GCPApplicationDefaultCredentials;
}

###BigQuery
BigQueryFunction <<fixture::bq::A.test>> {fixture::bq::A.val = 'ok'} fixture::bq::MyFunction
{
   functionName : 'MyFunction';
   function : zxx(Integer[1]):String[1];
   ownership : Deployment { identifier: 'myFunctionOwnership' };
   description : 'A super nice function!';
   activationConfiguration : fixture::bq::Conn;
}

BigQueryFunction fixture::bq::stage
{
   functionName : 'KeywordNamedFunction';
   function : zxx(Integer[1]):String[1];
}

BigQueryFunctionDeploymentConfiguration fixture::bq::Config
{
   activationConnection : fixture::bq::Conn;
}
